# Fedora: the machine issue #94 is actually about.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES, and it is one line of the installer: install_podman's `sudo apt-get update`
# (installer:591) on a machine with no apt. Everything before that point works -- platform()
# reports linux, the survey finds podman missing and asks permission for exactly one thing -- and
# then the install dies with "apt-get update failed", which is a true sentence about a machine
# that has never had apt and never will.
#
# PODMAN IS ABSENT BY OMISSION, NOT BY REMOVAL, which is why this fixture is small. The
# --no-prereqs axis removes software at boot and needs a file:// repository to put it back
# offline; here podman was simply never installed, so DO_PODMAN_INSTALL is yes on a machine that
# needs no local repo, no createrepo_c and no removal verb. When a Fedora case wants
# --no-prereqs, that machinery can be added then -- building the download closure for a case that
# does not exist yet is 300 MB of nothing.
#
# EXACTLY ONE CONSENT ITEM, which is the shape that makes the transcript readable, and it is the
# BASE IMAGE that gives it rather than anything below. Measured in fedora:43:
#
#   bash, sudo, curl, dnf         present     -- so none of them is a consent item
#   newuidmap, newgidmap, usermod present     -- shadow-utils is in the base image
#   ssh, ssh-keygen               ABSENT      -- installed below, or it would be a second item
#   /etc/subuid                   EMPTY       -- seeded below, or it would be a third item
#
# THE newuidmap LINE IS A FINDING, not a convenience. On Debian and Ubuntu the setuid helpers
# come from `uidmap`, a RECOMMENDS of podman, so "podman installed, helpers missing" is a real
# machine and the tier has a case for it. On Fedora they come from shadow-utils, which also owns
# usermod -- which setup_subuid needs -- so that state cannot be arranged here without breaking
# the machine, and it cannot occur on a student's Fedora box either. The case does not exist on
# this distro, and --no-prereqs=uidmap should be refused for this base rather than silently
# arranging nothing.
#
# TIER A -- NO NESTING ADAPTATIONS. uid 1000, a real subuid range, no vfs or cgroupfs override,
# and machine_flags hands this base no capabilities. Nothing here runs a podman, because the
# install dies before one exists to run.
# PINNED BY MANIFEST-LIST DIGEST, not a per-architecture one -- the same rule
# 00-release-gates.sh:143 states and asserts for the course image. An earlier pin here named
# the amd64 LEG of this index, which meant the fixture ran emulated on Apple Silicon; the
# emulated amd64 podman then SIGSEGVd inside the Go runtime's netpoll and the survey read a
# register dump where it expected a version. One digest, both legs, native on each.
FROM fedora:43@sha256:5025e03937bb59c0e69ecdbf2b7a94050add3aff0dbdbed1da5cd6aba62a6af0

# openssh-clients, NOT openssh-client -- Fedora's name for it, and the plural is exactly the kind
# of thing a fix for #94 has to get right per family. Deliberately NOT podman.
RUN dnf install -y openssh-clients \
 && dnf clean all

RUN if id -u 1000 >/dev/null 2>&1; then userdel -r "$(id -un 1000)" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; fi \
 && useradd -m -u 1000 -s /bin/bash student \
 && printf 'student ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL\n' > /etc/sudoers.d/student \
 && chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/student

# A range, so the subuid consent item cannot appear. fedora:43 ships an EMPTY /etc/subuid --
# Fedora's useradd populates it for users it creates, and the base image's file has no entries --
# so without this the survey would ask for two things and the transcript would be about the wrong
# one.
RUN printf 'student:200000:65536\n' > /etc/subuid \
 && printf 'student:200000:65536\n' > /etc/subgid

# The graph root's parent and the two tmpfs mount points, so mounting over them is not itself a
# change. Nothing here creates the first -- no podman ever runs -- but a fixture whose audit
# depends on that staying true is a fixture waiting to surprise somebody.
RUN mkdir -p /home/student/.local/share/containers && chown -R student:student /home/student/.local
RUN mkdir -p /var/tmp/shim /var/tmp/report && chmod 1777 /var/tmp/shim /var/tmp/report

USER student
WORKDIR /home/student
